> Medusa
> Once Medusa is dead, you get to view her statue safely.

Assuming you stoned her with reflection.  If you're reflecting and 
invisible, she won't stone herself.  

Furthermore, if you have reflection, you don't need blindness to protect 
yourself from Medusa's stoning attack (but why are you confronting her? 
Desperate for lev boots?).    

> If an Archaeologist, you will take an alignment hit if you
> break most of the statues on this level

*Only* her statue and Perseus' are historic.  Furthermore, -1 to 
alignment is not a "hit".  It is entirely meaningless, like almost every 
alignment penalty in the game, and certainly not worth distracting the 
reader with.


> The Castle

My experience is that usually I am too weak (AC, HP, weapon, intrinsics) 
to bull through the monsters, so I need a "trick":

- conflict
- chicken
- high level pet(s) + magic whistle
- Eye + good support spells (extra healing, sleep) or magic missile
- levitate around the back and let monsters fall down
- drawbridge

I know you mention conflict and rubber chickens in other places, but this 
is a good time to repeat it.  

> Vlad the Impaler
> his bite can drain levels.

...just like every vampire.  And just like every vampire, MC3 reduces the 
level drain chance to near-zero.  You aren't making it clear that he is a 
pushover.  http://www.alt.org/nethack/topdeaths.html
2405 ascensions.  One Vlad death, probably deliberate.

> Rodney's Tower

If you aren't already wearing conflict, now is a good time to put it on.  
Don't remove it until you reach your temple on Astral.  The other ring 
slot should default to free action, but switch to levitation or TC as 
needed.

> Moloch's Sanctum
> There are doors in and out of the graveyard. Use them to fight one
> monster at a time if your HP levels drop, or if you feel secure,
> bull through the mob the best way you can.

If your HP/AC are bad enough that the graveyard poses any threat at all, 
the priests and the HPOM are going to destroy you.

> The high priest has relatively poor armor (varies, AC:5 to AC:3),
 
Monster AC stopped being relevant about 30 dungeon levels ago.  You could 
mention that, like all priests, he has a chance at cloak of MR.

> but casts two spells and two physical attacks per turn.

The spells are the important thing.  He can be surprisingly dangerous.

> you will get zapped by Moloch when you hurt the high priest

...of course the lightning bolt will reflect harmlessly off you. 

> Plane of Air

This is a decent place to use the /SDD portal-finding method.

> If engulfed by an Air Elemental, try to take care of it quickly.
> With speed 36, it is at least twice as fast as you and hits with
> 1d10 each of its turns.

The danger is that (so far as I can tell) it ignores the damage reduction 
of negative AC.

> Plane of Water
> The slow method is to just stay in your air bubble.

AKA "the bad method".  Do you *want* Rodney to show up again?  The normal 
and correct method is to make your way to the portal with levitation.  If 
you're worried about sea monsters, genocide them.

Oddly enough, you can still pick items off the ground in the air bubbles 
while levitating.  Sometimes there is an item on top of the portal, so 
watch out. 

> Astral Plane

The pet angel is junk.  It will take him forever to clear any kind of a 
path for you.  On the other hand, a large crowd of charmed (as in the 
spell) pets can work well.  Use your magic whistle to keep them around 
you.  When you do have to fight, the cloud of pets will make sure only 
one or two monsters can get at you.  This is slow but pretty safe.  A 
fully leveled archon or mastodon might even kill the Riders for you.  

Of course conflict works fine instead.  There is an excellent chance that 
the Riders, who have low HP, will die before reaching you.  Conflict 
combines well with teleport wands, because instead of immediately filling 
the new gap, monsters will often stop to fight each other.

You can even use conflict and charm monster together.  A conflicted pet 
is no more dangerous than a conflicted enemy, and you can still displace 
it.  Unfortunately, some monsters become peaceful instead of tame, which 
means they're still in your way.  

> Make your way into the first temple - if the monsters get scared, you
> are in the right place.

If you've totally hosed your alignment (takes work; you pretty much have 
to murder a coaligned priest) you won't get sanctuary.  I guess this 
could count as trivia.

> do a last minute conversion.

HoOA only; you can't self-convert on the altar.





